=== clean | a bare slash is only a policy question under the uqf profile
x:1
/ a comment

=== QP002 profile: uqf | the legacy datetime type
t:2024.01.01T00:00:00.000

=== clean profile: uqf | a timestamp has the precision uqf wants
t:2024.01.01D00:00:00.000000000

=== QP001 profile: uqf | a terminated block comment is still policy, not syntax
/
text
\

=== QP003 profile: uqf | the wall-clock timestamp where UTC is the convention
t:.z.P

=== clean profile: uqf | UTC temporals are what the profile asks for
t:.z.p

=== QP005 profile: uqf | multiplication mixed with addition relies on evaluation order
r:2*3+4

=== clean profile: uqf | parenthesised, the order is said out loud
r:(2*3)+4

=== clean profile: uqf | a single operator family is unambiguous
r:2*3*4

=== clean | dynamic evaluation turns checks off without that being a defect
v:value "x"

=== clean | a load is dynamic too
\l utils.q

=== clean | eval is dynamic
r:eval parse "1+1"

=== clean | a load through system is dynamic
system "l utils.q"

=== clean | value on a dictionary reads it, nothing is evaluated
r:value `a`b!1 2

=== clean | value on a lambda decomposes it
r:value {x+1}

=== clean | system with a shell command defines no names
system "mkdir -p out"

=== clean | set with a symbol literal is a definition the file spells out, and the global is known
`cfg set 1
f:{[a] a+cfg}

=== QF014 | the local-scope rule runs even where the file evaluates dynamically
v:value "x"
f:{[x] r:cfg; cfg:1; r}

=== clean | dynamic evaluation still skips the undefined-global check that would say 'x
v:value "x"
f:{[a] a+x}

=== QF010 | without it, the same lambda draws the check
f:{[a] a+x}

=== QP001 QE003 profile: uqf | a bare slash at column 0 opens a block comment, and nothing closes it
a:1
/

=== clean profile: uqf | an indented slash does not: q keeps reading code after it
a:1
  /

=== QP006 profile: uqf | a function this file defines, applied without brackets
f:{x+1}
r:f 2

=== clean profile: uqf | the same call with the brackets the convention asks for
f:{x+1}
r:f[2]

=== clean | juxtaposition is only a policy question under the uqf profile
f:{x+1}
r:f 2

=== clean profile: uqf | a builtin reads better without brackets, and is not this rule's business
f:{x+1}
r:count "abc"

=== clean profile: uqf | a name this file never defines as a lambda might be a dictionary or a list
r:lookup `a

=== clean profile: uqf | a name assigned something other than a lambda is indexed, not called
t:`a`b!1 2
r:t `a

=== QP006 profile: uqf | a namespaced function, and the argument runs to the end of the expression
.ns.scale:{x*2}
r:.ns.scale 3+4

=== clean profile: uqf | an adverb applies to the function, it does not call it
f:{x+1}
r:f each 1 2 3

=== clean profile: uqf | an infix builtin puts the function on the left of an operator
f:{x+1}
r:f in `a`b

=== clean profile: uqf | a local of the same name says nothing about the global
f:{x+1}
g:{[f] f 2}

=== clean profile: uqf | a system command's argument is not an argument
d:{x+1}
\d .ns

=== QP006 profile: uqf | a call at the head of its own line
step:{x+1}
step 1
